1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:16,660
In my previous life, were my parents worried about me?

2
00:00:17,580 --> 00:00:22,480
Just before they died, how did they feel about their son, the shut-in?

3
00:00:23,440 --> 00:00:24,500
I'll never know.

4
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:26,800
I didn't go to their funeral.

5
00:00:27,660 --> 00:00:29,840
Didn't collect their ashes like a son should.

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,000
What the hell was I doing?

7
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:36,000
I barely loved my parents.

8
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:39,000
It pressures me to think about how little I cared for them.

9
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:41,000
I should have been there, right?

10
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:43,000
Should have gone to the funeral.

11
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Seen their dead faces.

12
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:47,000
Give them one last goodbye.

13
00:00:47,000 --> 00:01:02,000
If you were gonna die, it should have been for Norn and Aisha.

14
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:04,000
Not a fake like me.

15
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:08,000
And then there's Zenith and Lilia.

16
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:12,000
How could you go and abandon all four of them like this?

17
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:13,000
They were your everything.

18
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Didn't they mean the world to you?

19
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:16,000
Damn it, Paul.

20
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:17,000
What the hell am I supposed to do now?

21
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:18,000
I need you to tell me.

22
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:19,000
My boy.

23
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:21,000
I'm so lucky to have a son like you.

24
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:22,000
To be honest, I never truly felt like his son.

25
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:26,000
But Paul Greyrat was always my father.

26
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:28,000
Hey Rudy, mind if I come in?

27
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:29,000
Mind if I come in?

28
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:30,000
I'm so lucky to have a son like you.

29
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:31,000
I'm so lucky to have a son like you.

30
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:35,000
To be honest, I never truly felt like his son.

31
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:37,000
But Paul Greyrat was always my father.

32
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:56,000
Hey Rudy, mind if I come in?

33
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Of course not.

34
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:04,000
If you're up to it, maybe we should go for a walk.

35
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:05,000
Huh?

36
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:10,000
Just think, this city has loads of magical items you can't find anywhere else.

37
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:12,000
Why don't we go explore?

38
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:14,000
Check out the shops like we did the other day?

39
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:16,000
No thanks.

40
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:18,000
I'm not in the mood.

41
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:21,000
Oh, I understand.

42
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:23,000
Sorry, Master.

43
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:45,000
I know it's tough.

44
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:48,000
What happened to Paul and Zenith in there is a real tragedy.

45
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:54,000
I still fondly remember the five of us living together in Buena Village all those years ago.

46
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:59,000
Truthfully, those days may have been the happiest in my entire life.

47
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:09,000
When we go out on adventures, sometimes we end up losing people, even the ones who are closest to us.

48
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:11,000
It's never easy.

49
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:12,000
I know.

50
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:14,000
I've gone through it myself.

51
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:17,000
Master, I wish you wouldn't lie to me.

52
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:21,000
Your mother and father are still out there alive and well, aren't they?

53
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:22,000
You're right.

54
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:23,000
They're both alive.

55
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:28,000
It's been a few years since I've seen them at this point, but they seem to be-

56
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:29,000
Then you don't know anything!

57
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:32,000
So don't sit there and pretend like you do, okay?

58
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:36,000
It just occurred to me.

59
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:41,000
I thought I'd start it over, like I was finally getting it right.

60
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:46,000
But turns out I was still ignoring everything that actually matters.

61
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:49,000
Anytime we'd fight, I'd just run away from them.

62
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:53,000
I just kept making all the same mistakes that I can never take back.

63
00:03:57,000 --> 00:04:00,000
I thought I'd changed.

64
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:04,000
But in the end, I'm still the same person I've always been.

65
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:09,000
Of course you're the same person.

66
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:11,000
Still bursting with talent.

67
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:14,000
You're still kind, just like Paul and Xenath taught you to be.

68
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:18,000
You all welcomed me into your home and gave me a place to belong.

69
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:24,000
Thanks to you three, I learned what the true embrace of a real family felt like.

70
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:29,000
Sure we weren't blood, but your mom and dad, we're my family too.

71
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:31,000
We're my family too.

72
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:42,000
Rudy, please let me feel the weight of the sadness with you.

73
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:44,000
Please.

74
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:52,000
I may be small and inadequate, but I'm still your teacher.

75
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:55,000
I've lived a lot longer and it's given me more time to toughen up.

76
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:58,000
Believe me, I know the ache of despair.

77
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:03,000
And I know it hurts, but it can hurt less if you share the pain.

78
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:04,000
The pain.

79
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:07,000
Rudy!

80
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:23,000
Please rest.

81
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:29,000
For now, just leave everything to your master.

82
00:05:53,000 --> 00:06:16,000
Oh, Rudy, good morning.

83
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:20,000
Yeah, good morning, master.

84
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:24,000
So, uh, do you feel any better than you did last night?

85
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:27,000
I do.

86
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:38,000
Hey, master.

87
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:41,000
Would you be okay with me asking a strange question?

88
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:42,000
Go ahead.

89
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:46,000
If I felt like a bad son, what should I do now?

90
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:53,000
Well, I would focus on the family you have left and do right by them.

91
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:58,000
If Po were still here, I'm certain that's what he would have wanted.

92
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:00,000
Not to wallow in this.

93
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:02,000
For your family's sake.

94
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:03,000
You're right.

95
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:07,000
Master, thank you for everything.

96
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:08,000
Sure.

97
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:09,000
Hey, Roxy, did you?

98
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:10,000
I'm sorry.

99
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:11,000
Could you give us a few minutes?

100
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:12,000
She and I have matters we need to discuss.

101
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:13,000
You go on ahead and join Miss Lelia.

102
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:14,000
Yeah, understood.

103
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:15,000
I'm sorry.

104
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:17,000
Could you give us a few minutes?

105
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:18,000
Oh, what can I do?

106
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:20,000
You go on ahead and join Miss Lelia.

107
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:21,000
Yeah, understood.

108
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:26,000
Okay.

109
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:29,000
Can you tell us somebody that's not the best?

110
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:30,000
Hey, Roxy, did you…

111
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:33,000
I'm sorry.

112
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:34,000
Could you give us a few minutes?

113
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:37,000
She and I have matters we need to discuss.

114
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:39,000
You go on ahead and join Miss Lelia.

115
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:41,000
Yeah.

116
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:42,000
Understood.

117
00:07:47,000 --> 00:08:02,540
Good morning, Leilia.

118
00:08:03,140 --> 00:08:05,020
Is something the matter, Master Rudeus?

119
00:08:05,480 --> 00:08:09,400
It's just that I'm sorry you've had to care for her without me.

120
00:08:09,960 --> 00:08:12,000
Oh, don't be. This is my duty.

121
00:08:14,720 --> 00:08:16,800
How is she? Any progress?

122
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:21,480
Well, she doesn't seem to remember anything, but physically she is quite healthy.

123
00:08:22,240 --> 00:08:24,020
No residual impairment otherwise.

124
00:08:24,280 --> 00:08:24,940
Is that so?

125
00:08:27,020 --> 00:08:30,140
She just lost her memory. I guess that's good.

126
00:08:30,940 --> 00:08:32,960
It's not like she's completely brain dead.

127
00:08:33,860 --> 00:08:37,980
Shiera has her own pet theory, that this is a side effect being trapped in the crystal.

128
00:08:38,520 --> 00:08:40,220
Something akin to mana poisoning.

129
00:08:42,620 --> 00:08:43,800
Will she recover?

130
00:08:43,800 --> 00:08:50,540
Well, sir, if Alina Lee speaks the truth, there's little hope for that.

131
00:08:50,540 --> 00:08:57,580
My lady treated me like family for many years.

132
00:08:57,580 --> 00:09:02,860
Now that my lord has passed on, it would be my honor to care for her in this time of need.

133
00:09:02,860 --> 00:09:06,420
Thank you. I'll do whatever I can, too.

134
00:09:07,060 --> 00:09:08,280
That's not necessary.

135
00:09:08,560 --> 00:09:08,920
What?

136
00:09:09,580 --> 00:09:13,420
Please forgive me, sir. I realize I'm overstepping my bounds.

137
00:09:14,080 --> 00:09:17,440
But will you allow me to speak freely, impolite or otherwise at this time?

138
00:09:18,300 --> 00:09:18,800
Please.

139
00:09:18,800 --> 00:09:23,520
From now on, focus on your own duties.

140
00:09:24,400 --> 00:09:26,360
I don't understand. Why?

141
00:09:27,180 --> 00:09:28,840
It's what your father would have wanted.

142
00:09:29,940 --> 00:09:32,740
My duty is right here, at my lady's side.

143
00:09:33,520 --> 00:09:35,840
You have a family now, and they need you.

144
00:09:42,620 --> 00:09:43,540
Let's go home.

145
00:09:44,380 --> 00:09:45,580
They're waiting for us.

146
00:09:45,580 --> 00:10:15,560
You have a family now, and they're waiting for us.

147
00:10:15,580 --> 00:10:17,900
You have a family now, and they're waiting for us.

148
00:10:17,980 --> 00:10:19,940
You have a family now, and they're waiting for us.

149
00:10:20,400 --> 00:10:21,480
Thank you, sir.

150
00:10:21,480 --> 00:10:22,300
Thank you, sir.

151
00:10:22,480 --> 00:10:23,160
Thank you.

152
00:10:27,120 --> 00:10:27,840
Thank you.

153
00:10:27,840 --> 00:10:57,820
Thank you.

154
00:10:57,840 --> 00:11:03,940
Master, we need to talk.

155
00:11:04,480 --> 00:11:06,500
Yes, of course, Rudy. What is it?

156
00:11:08,760 --> 00:11:11,500
Let's be honest. I love Roxy.

157
00:11:12,660 --> 00:11:17,700
Not in quite the same way I love Sylphie, but I couldn't tell you who I love more.

158
00:11:18,880 --> 00:11:22,920
So I'm torn. I love my wife, and I love my master.

159
00:11:22,920 --> 00:11:30,800
But I gave Sylphie my word that I'd stay faithful. I can't betray that.

160
00:11:32,020 --> 00:11:36,220
You deserve to know. Before all this happened, I actually got married.

161
00:11:37,020 --> 00:11:38,780
In fact, we have a child on the way.

162
00:11:39,800 --> 00:11:43,100
So I'm... I'm really sorry for giving you any false hope.

163
00:11:43,100 --> 00:11:46,600
But romance isn't really...

164
00:11:46,600 --> 00:11:51,820
I know all that. After your dad passed away, and we were all worried about your well-being,

165
00:11:52,460 --> 00:11:54,480
Alina Lise told me a lot about your life.

166
00:11:55,060 --> 00:11:56,340
Really? Then why?

167
00:11:56,340 --> 00:12:01,020
Please don't blame yourself. You were so upset.

168
00:12:01,540 --> 00:12:04,820
I took advantage of the situation to help us both feel a little better.

169
00:12:05,600 --> 00:12:07,220
It was entirely my decision.

170
00:12:07,860 --> 00:12:12,340
And besides, if you had the choice, I know you wouldn't normally go for someone like me.

171
00:12:12,760 --> 00:12:13,940
It's not like that.

172
00:12:13,940 --> 00:12:21,740
Don't worry. I have no plans to barge into your life. I'll just be your left hand.

173
00:12:22,540 --> 00:12:26,340
And then once we get back home, you can give your wife all your devotion.

174
00:12:28,380 --> 00:12:31,820
If that's what you want. Can I at least repay you, though?

175
00:12:32,280 --> 00:12:34,340
You want to repay me? For what?

176
00:12:34,640 --> 00:12:37,680
Well, for everything that you've done for me.

177
00:12:37,680 --> 00:12:44,680
Huh? I see. All right, then. Would you like to start by listening to my excuse?

178
00:12:45,040 --> 00:12:46,720
Um, excuse for what?

179
00:12:47,160 --> 00:12:48,720
All you have to do is listen.

180
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:50,880
Okay. Please, go ahead.

181
00:12:53,100 --> 00:12:56,220
I fell in love at first sight.

182
00:12:56,840 --> 00:12:57,620
With whom?

183
00:12:59,860 --> 00:13:04,000
With you, Rudy. The very moment you came to my rescue in the labyrinth.

184
00:13:04,380 --> 00:13:04,760
Really?

185
00:13:04,760 --> 00:13:09,280
Why are you surprised? An entrance like that would make anyone's heart race.

186
00:13:10,600 --> 00:13:15,100
You were the picture of my ideal partner the entire time we were down there.

187
00:13:15,740 --> 00:13:17,480
I couldn't take my eyes off of you.

188
00:13:18,060 --> 00:13:20,040
You wouldn't even look me in the eye, though.

189
00:13:20,480 --> 00:13:23,580
I know. Can you blame me? I was nervous.

190
00:13:25,120 --> 00:13:27,200
I thought the whole thing was hopeless.

191
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:29,700
And then once we got back to the inn,

192
00:13:30,420 --> 00:13:33,040
Elena, Lisa, and Geese thought you'd be fine on your own.

193
00:13:33,040 --> 00:13:37,520
But I remembered what you were like as a kid in Buena.

194
00:13:42,320 --> 00:13:46,640
Uh, of course I had been told that you shared your life with someone you love.

195
00:13:47,020 --> 00:13:50,940
And if you felt broken, I knew she'd have the power to lift you back up.

196
00:13:50,940 --> 00:13:55,960
Only, she wasn't here when you needed her most.

197
00:13:55,960 --> 00:13:59,960
So, I felt like someone had to save you.

198
00:14:00,280 --> 00:14:03,660
Even if Elena, Lisa, and Geese thought it best to leave you alone.

199
00:14:04,300 --> 00:14:05,180
And poor Lelia.

200
00:14:05,800 --> 00:14:07,940
I knew she wouldn't have the time or energy,

201
00:14:08,460 --> 00:14:10,500
since she had her hands full with zenith.

202
00:14:11,300 --> 00:14:14,620
So, to ease your pain, I did what I thought was right.

203
00:14:14,620 --> 00:14:18,000
In the end, I couldn't help it.

204
00:14:19,500 --> 00:14:20,780
I love you.

205
00:14:20,780 --> 00:14:26,960
I was being selfish.

206
00:14:27,480 --> 00:14:29,000
I should have loved you alone.

207
00:14:30,280 --> 00:14:31,840
Master, listen to me.

208
00:14:31,840 --> 00:14:35,780
What is it?

209
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:40,100
While we're here, at least before we make it home.

210
00:14:41,240 --> 00:14:41,760
No.

211
00:14:42,240 --> 00:14:43,300
What good will that do?

212
00:14:43,680 --> 00:14:44,780
It doesn't solve anything.

213
00:14:45,460 --> 00:14:47,540
Not for me, and certainly not for Roxy.

214
00:14:47,540 --> 00:14:57,440
That's enough.

215
00:14:57,820 --> 00:14:58,840
I'll be fine.

216
00:14:59,600 --> 00:15:01,140
I don't need you to do anything.

217
00:15:03,880 --> 00:15:05,080
Okay, I'll stop.

218
00:15:17,540 --> 00:15:24,300
You can remove your blindfolds now.

219
00:15:24,440 --> 00:15:25,300
We've made it outside.

220
00:15:28,400 --> 00:15:30,160
Rudy, where are we?

221
00:15:30,840 --> 00:15:32,640
We're in a forest near Sharia.

222
00:15:33,320 --> 00:15:34,340
I can't believe it.

223
00:15:34,700 --> 00:15:36,580
We've really made it to the Northlands already?

224
00:15:37,440 --> 00:15:38,780
Now I get it, boss.

225
00:15:39,100 --> 00:15:41,120
I see how you got to Rapun so fast.

226
00:15:41,260 --> 00:15:44,460
Whatever you do, don't tell anyone about this place.

227
00:15:44,580 --> 00:15:45,160
Sure thing.

228
00:15:45,520 --> 00:15:45,860
Okay.

229
00:15:45,860 --> 00:15:48,460
Elina, Lys, and I will take the lead from here.

230
00:16:04,120 --> 00:16:04,560
Rudeus?

231
00:16:04,980 --> 00:16:05,580
What's up?

232
00:16:06,160 --> 00:16:06,780
Your faith.

233
00:16:07,140 --> 00:16:09,400
You're not a worshiper of Mili's now, are you?

234
00:16:10,500 --> 00:16:11,660
I never have been.

235
00:16:12,340 --> 00:16:14,860
And would it be safe to assume that Sylphie isn't either?

236
00:16:14,860 --> 00:16:17,200
Yeah, that'd be a safe bet.

237
00:16:18,100 --> 00:16:21,260
As you know, my dear Cliff is a devout follower.

238
00:16:21,780 --> 00:16:22,080
Mm-hmm.

239
00:16:23,280 --> 00:16:28,260
What you may not know is that followers of Mili's are only allowed to take one wife.

240
00:16:28,960 --> 00:16:34,120
It's meant to be a lifelong commitment, and they are to remain faithful to her till death do they part.

241
00:16:34,120 --> 00:16:35,300
It's a bit strict.

242
00:16:35,300 --> 00:16:40,980
It's a bit strict, but now that I'm on the receiving end, I must admit I rather enjoy it.

243
00:16:41,600 --> 00:16:49,800
That being said, in my opinion, there is absolutely nothing wrong with loving more than one partner at the same time.

244
00:16:49,800 --> 00:16:56,800
I'm not surprised, but what exactly are you trying to say?

245
00:16:56,800 --> 00:17:01,200
To be clear, I think you should marry Roxy.

246
00:17:01,200 --> 00:17:04,940
Are you being serious right now?

247
00:17:05,720 --> 00:17:06,080
Yes.

248
00:17:06,500 --> 00:17:10,380
With every fiber of me, no one else could mean it like I do.

249
00:17:12,020 --> 00:17:15,580
Frankly, I can't stand to see Roxy like this.

250
00:17:16,440 --> 00:17:17,400
The poor girl.

251
00:17:17,400 --> 00:17:25,700
She yearns to throw herself into the relationship with you, but she's forcing herself to hold back just because she met you at the wrong time.

252
00:17:26,760 --> 00:17:29,620
I want Roxy to have a modest share of happiness.

253
00:17:30,440 --> 00:17:32,700
At the very least, she deserves that.

254
00:17:32,780 --> 00:17:34,760
Yeah, but what about Sylphie?

255
00:17:34,760 --> 00:17:36,700
What do you plan to do about Roxy, then?

256
00:17:37,540 --> 00:17:39,620
Of course, I want her to be happy, too.

257
00:17:40,360 --> 00:17:41,740
I want that for both of them.

258
00:17:42,360 --> 00:17:44,200
It's just that I made a promise.

259
00:17:44,200 --> 00:17:49,020
How selfish can I be?

260
00:17:49,680 --> 00:17:51,000
I married Sylphie.

261
00:17:51,120 --> 00:17:52,160
We have a kid on the way.

262
00:17:52,720 --> 00:17:54,400
And now I want another woman, too?

263
00:17:56,120 --> 00:18:02,600
To think all those times I've called Paul a scumbag, and now I'm sitting here contemplating the same thing.

264
00:18:03,600 --> 00:18:04,900
What about Paul and Lelia?

265
00:18:05,440 --> 00:18:09,180
After their affair and subsequent marriage, did Zenith become miserable?

266
00:18:14,200 --> 00:18:32,440
No, other than some tears and resentment at first.

267
00:18:32,440 --> 00:18:35,180
Well, sure, that much goes without saying.

268
00:18:35,840 --> 00:18:37,460
I know you've got it in you.

269
00:18:38,080 --> 00:18:40,920
You can love Sylphie and Roxy all the same, boy.

270
00:18:41,900 --> 00:18:43,400
You're Paul's flesh and blood.

271
00:18:44,040 --> 00:18:46,300
He must be at least good for that, wouldn't you agree?

272
00:18:47,480 --> 00:18:48,380
Maybe so.

273
00:18:48,860 --> 00:18:50,980
I genuinely love them both.

274
00:18:50,980 --> 00:18:55,060
But what would Sylphie think if I came home with a lover?

275
00:18:57,060 --> 00:18:58,340
And what about Roxy?

276
00:18:59,160 --> 00:19:01,100
She might want me all to herself.

277
00:19:01,860 --> 00:19:05,240
Or what if they both dump me and I wind up alone again?

278
00:19:06,320 --> 00:19:09,440
I want to be able to give them the lives they deserve.

279
00:19:12,360 --> 00:19:13,180
I guess.

280
00:19:13,760 --> 00:19:19,740
But even if I want to go through with it, they'd both have to be in agreement, and that might be a different story altogether.

281
00:19:19,740 --> 00:19:24,260
In that case, you should find out what Roxy's feelings are, huh?

282
00:19:24,260 --> 00:19:25,260
Look.

283
00:19:27,760 --> 00:19:36,260
Hey.

284
00:19:44,560 --> 00:19:46,360
What do you want to talk about?

285
00:19:47,460 --> 00:19:48,580
Master...

286
00:19:48,580 --> 00:19:51,400
This is something I've wanted to say for a long time.

287
00:19:53,600 --> 00:19:54,160
Okay.

288
00:19:57,320 --> 00:20:00,640
Throughout my adventures, your teachings saved my life.

289
00:20:01,640 --> 00:20:04,740
Without your influence, I wouldn't have made it this far.

290
00:20:06,120 --> 00:20:07,740
So, I guess...

291
00:20:08,980 --> 00:20:10,120
Well, here's the thing.

292
00:20:11,040 --> 00:20:12,920
I'm married to someone dear to me.

293
00:20:13,980 --> 00:20:16,680
Her name's Sylphiet Greyrat, and we're expecting a child.

294
00:20:17,260 --> 00:20:19,100
I know. We talked about it.

295
00:20:20,200 --> 00:20:22,180
What the hell am I trying to say here?

296
00:20:23,140 --> 00:20:24,320
My, uh...

297
00:20:24,320 --> 00:20:25,820
My wife...

298
00:20:25,820 --> 00:20:27,720
She didn't used to have a family name.

299
00:20:28,300 --> 00:20:29,860
She was always just Sylphiet.

300
00:20:30,980 --> 00:20:33,180
Yes. I'm aware of that, too.

301
00:20:33,680 --> 00:20:35,860
That's not what I wanted to say at all!

302
00:20:41,680 --> 00:20:42,640
Oh, fine.

303
00:20:43,140 --> 00:20:45,940
Being a scumbag beats looking back and wishing I'd said more.

304
00:20:45,940 --> 00:20:46,780
Sure, right?

305
00:20:48,360 --> 00:20:53,020
Master Roxy, would you ever consider changing your full name to Roxy Greyrat?

306
00:20:53,520 --> 00:20:53,940
Uh...

307
00:20:54,940 --> 00:20:57,940
I love you, too.

308
00:20:57,940 --> 00:21:13,560
I'm grateful to hear you say that.

309
00:21:13,920 --> 00:21:14,800
Truly, I am.

310
00:21:15,940 --> 00:21:16,440
But...

311
00:21:16,440 --> 00:21:19,440
A decision like this would require your wife's approval.

312
00:21:20,280 --> 00:21:21,620
Without a doubt, yes.

313
00:21:21,620 --> 00:21:23,620
Well, then...

314
00:21:25,620 --> 00:21:27,580
No.

315
00:21:28,280 --> 00:21:30,540
But please ask again what she's given it.

316
00:21:30,540 --> 00:21:31,540
Uh...

317
00:21:31,540 --> 00:21:42,540
I...

318
00:21:42,540 --> 00:21:43,200
Okay.

319
00:21:43,200 --> 00:22:00,320
What do you know?

320
00:22:00,900 --> 00:22:01,740
We're the same.

321
00:22:01,740 --> 00:22:02,960
What do you know?

322
00:22:02,960 --> 00:22:03,200
That one...

323
00:22:03,200 --> 00:22:03,860
The Saucong...

324
00:22:03,860 --> 00:22:03,980
I love you.

325
00:22:04,800 --> 00:22:05,420
I love you.

326
00:22:05,420 --> 00:22:06,720
I love you.

327
00:22:06,840 --> 00:22:07,220
My mom.

328
00:22:08,340 --> 00:22:08,520
Be sure to fit.

329
00:22:08,520 --> 00:22:08,720
You know?

330
00:22:09,220 --> 00:22:10,060
Go get her born.

331
00:22:10,440 --> 00:22:10,980
Come Wam.

332
00:22:10,980 --> 00:22:11,660
Come.

333
00:22:11,900 --> 00:22:12,300
I love you.

334
00:22:12,640 --> 00:22:13,240
What do you know?

335
00:22:13,460 --> 00:22:15,060
I love you.

336
00:22:15,160 --> 00:22:15,780
You know how I truly meet you.

337
00:22:15,780 --> 00:22:16,580
How do you know how to do the right thing?

338
00:23:35,940 --> 00:23:39,940
La-ya-la-ya-la

